# Step 27, the named pipe of `serve --socket` on Windows: who may open it,
# and the check of each connection's own token, broken one at a time
# (docs/steps/27/answered.md, "The design, before building", point 1,
# "Windows"). Windows builds this code alone: run the breaks on a runner,
# `gh workflow run try --ref <branch> -f os=windows -f
# command="mutate step-27-pipe --jobs 2"`.

# ------------------------------------------------------- the pipe's security

[break] pipe-label-lets-a-lower-process-write
rule: The pipe is labelled at the server's integrity with no write up: a process below it cannot open the pipe to write.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: description
in-string: ML;;NWNR;;;S-1-16
replace: ML;;NR;;;S-1-16
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::a_client_below_the_servers_integrity_is_kept_out
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::the_pipe_admits_the_user_alone_at_the_servers_integrity

[break] pipe-label-lets-a-lower-process-read
rule: The pipe's label has no read up as well: a process below the server's integrity cannot open the pipe to read, where it could hold a connection it never writes on and so is never checked.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: description
in-string: ML;;NWNR;;;S-1-16
replace: ML;;NW;;;S-1-16
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::a_client_below_the_servers_integrity_is_kept_out
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::the_pipe_admits_the_user_alone_at_the_servers_integrity

[break] pipe-access-list-admits-everyone
rule: The pipe's access list allows the user alone: another user cannot open it.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: description
in-string: D:P(A;;GA;;;{user})S:
replace: D:P(A;;GA;;;{user})(A;;GRGW;;;WD)S:
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::the_pipe_admits_the_user_alone_at_the_servers_integrity
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::sys_another_user_cannot_open_the_pipe

[break] pipe-access-list-not-protected
rule: The pipe's access list is protected from inheritance: it holds the entry it was made with and nothing else.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: description
in-string: D:P(A;;GA;;;{user})S:
replace: D:(A;;GA;;;{user})S:
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::the_pipe_admits_the_user_alone_at_the_servers_integrity

[break] pipe-widened-without-asking
rule: Everyone is let at the pipe only by a test's own listener that asks for it; every other pipe is the user's alone.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: Listener::bind
find: description(server, widened(options))
replace: description(server, true)
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::the_pipe_admits_the_user_alone_at_the_servers_integrity
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::sys_another_user_cannot_open_the_pipe

[break] pipe-first-instance-joins-a-name-in-use
rule: The first instance is made only where no instance of the name exists: a second server, or a pipe another process holds at the name, refuses the start.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: instance
find: let first = if first {
replace: let first = if false {
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::a_name_in_use_is_refused

[break] pipe-name-lapses-between-instances
rule: The next instance is made before a connected one is handed on, so the name never lapses and an instance always waits for the next client.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: Listener::hand_to_check
find:
    let next = registered(instance(&self.name, &self.description, false)?)?;
    let connected = self.waiting.replace(next).ok_or_else(gone)?;
replace:
    let connected = self.waiting.take().ok_or_else(gone)?;
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::a_silent_client_holds_up_no_other_and_the_name_never_lapses

[break] pipe-silent-clients-are-kept
rule: Past the most connections that may wait for their first data, the one that has waited longest is closed, so that clients that never write cannot hold the pipe's instances.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: Listener::hand_to_check
find: oldest.abort();
replace: let _ = oldest;
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::the_longest_silent_client_is_closed_to_make_room

[break] pipe-first-data-is-dropped
rule: What was read of a client for the check of its token is handed on first, once it is admitted: nothing it sent is lost.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: admit
find: let read = std::io::Cursor::new(first).chain(read);
replace: let read = std::io::Cursor::new(Vec::new()).chain(read);
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::a_silent_client_holds_up_no_other_and_the_name_never_lapses

[break] pipe-default-is-one-name-for-every-user
rule: The default pipe is named for the user's security identifier, so that two users' servers do not meet at one name.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: default_place
in-string: cortex-harness-{user}
replace: cortex-harness
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc socket::sys::tests::the_default_pipe_is_named_for_the_user

# -------------------------------------------- the check of a client's token

[break] pipe-another-users-token-admitted
rule: A connection whose token is another user's is refused by the check of its token, even where the pipe let it open.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: check
find: if user != server.user {
replace: if user != server.user && false {
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::sys_another_user_cannot_open_the_pipe

[break] pipe-lower-integrity-admitted
rule: A connection whose token is below the server's integrity is refused.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: check
find: if level < server.level {
replace: if level < server.level && false {
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::a_client_below_the_servers_integrity_is_kept_out

[break] pipe-restricted-token-admitted
rule: A connection whose token is restricted is refused.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: check
find: if is_restricted(token).map_err(unread)? {
replace: if is_restricted(token).map_err(unread)? && false {
os: windows
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it pipe::a_restricted_client_is_refused

[break] pipe-app-container-admitted
rule: A connection whose token is an AppContainer's is refused. No test sees this break alone: an AppContainer's token is at low integrity, which the integrity check refuses first, and making one in a test needs a container profile and a process started in it.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/socket/windows.rs
in: check
find: if is_app_container(token).map_err(unread)? {
replace: if is_app_container(token).map_err(unread)? && false {
os: windows
expect: survives
